      "id": 1,
      "text": "Auderghem became an independent municipality in 1863 after centuries of being part of a single village with Watermael and Boitsfort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8,
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auderghem",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1956, Paul Henri Spaak hosted the Intergovernmental Conference at the Château of Val Duchesse, sparking the Treaties of Rome.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auderghem",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Auderghem lies in southeastern Brussels, along the Woluwe valley and at the entrance to the Sonian Forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auderghem",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Like all Brussels municipalities, Auderghem is legally bilingual, offering services in both French and Dutch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auderghem",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Priory of Val Duchesse, a royal gift, is rarely open to the public, preserving its historic charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auderghem",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Auderghem preserves a rich natural and historic legacy, including creeks, Rouge Cloître Abbey, the Priory, Château of Trois-Fontaines, and a chapel.",
